  "reason": "Evidence: config_004 (scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted, multiprofile) achieved the best accuracy (0.713) and clearly outperformed config_048 (same setup but avgpool aggregation, 0.678), confirming transformer aggregation is critical for multiprofile settings. The remaining uncertainty is whether the fusion strategy (weighted vs concat) interacts with transformer aggregation to further improve accuracy. This experiment (config_024) isolates that single variable—switching fusion from weighted to concat while keeping everything else identical to the best config. It is the cheapest logical extension (~6.2 GPU hrs, comparable to config_004 since it uses the same encoders and transformer aggregation), making it an efficient use of budget. If concat improves accuracy, it opens a promising direction for combining with stronger image encoders in later experiments; if not, it confirms weighted fusion is optimal and frees remaining budget for testing imagenet_vit_l or scgpt. With 7 experiments still available, this low-cost, high-information experiment is the best next step before committing to more expensive architectural changes."
